1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:05,730
The Senate Committee on
Agriculture and Cooperatives

2
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:10,360
held Meeting No. 37/2569 on
Monday, 2 November 2026.

3
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:15,120
Mr. Sountorn Chaokijka, the committee
chair, presided over the meeting.

4
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,741
The meeting considered extending
the fishing zone line in Krabi

5
00:00:19,741 --> 00:00:23,850
province, to ease hardship for
fishers around Koh Sriboya

6
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:27,959
in Nuea Khlong district and
Koh Po in Koh Lanta district.

7
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:32,657
Small-scale fishers in the
area report that their fishing

8
00:00:32,657 --> 00:00:35,899
gear has been damaged by
commercial fishing boats.

9
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:41,238
They want the no-fishing zone
extended for trawls, push nets,

10
00:00:41,238 --> 00:00:45,979
shellfish dredges and night-time
anchovy light fishing.

11
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:50,504
The committee therefore invited the
Department of Fisheries and the Krabi

12
00:00:50,504 --> 00:00:54,339
Fishers Association to the meeting,
to seek solutions together.

13
00:00:55,340 --> 00:01:00,346
The Krabi Fishers Association
said it faces limits on

14
00:01:00,346 --> 00:01:04,879
fishing grounds and
declining aquatic resources.

15
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:09,197
It proposes extending the fishing
zone from about 3 nautical miles

16
00:01:09,197 --> 00:01:13,370
to 9 nautical miles, following the
area and natural island lines.

17
00:01:13,451 --> 00:01:19,062
This would not bar fishers from
other provinces; it aims for all

18
00:01:19,062 --> 00:01:24,059
sides to share aquatic resources
under suitable measures.

19
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:28,740
The Department of Fisheries
explained that the impact

20
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:32,420
on fishers from several
provinces must be considered,

21
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:36,100
especially Trang and Krabi,
which share the sea area.

22
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:41,399
And extending a fishing zone is a power
of the Minister under the fisheries law.

23
00:01:41,479 --> 00:01:46,976
It has gathered the necessary data,
and will submit the matter to the

24
00:01:46,976 --> 00:01:52,473
committee on aquatic resource
conservation measures by December 2026.

25
00:01:52,553 --> 00:01:57,920
It will then follow the legal steps
to issue an enforceable notification.

26
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:03,565
Members said the decision should
balance conserving aquatic

27
00:02:03,565 --> 00:02:07,344
resources with protecting
fishers' right to make

28
00:02:07,344 --> 00:02:11,359
a living, and seek a solution
all sides can accept.

29
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:15,121
And while the notification is
pending, there should be urgent

30
00:02:15,121 --> 00:02:18,199
measures the Department can
take under current law.

31
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:22,830
The meeting resolved to ask the
Department of Fisheries to report

32
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:26,680
its outcome and progress to
the committee, to follow up

33
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:30,740
on the issue, and to inform
the Krabi Fishers Association.

34
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:36,100
The committee's three current
subcommittees are chaired as follows.

35
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:39,740
Livestock and Fisheries:
Mr. Ruchu Kaewlai.

36
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:46,000
Water Management in Farm Areas Outside
Irrigation Zones: Miss Amorn Sribunnak.

37
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:50,420
And Integrated Agricultural
Networks: Mr. Choocheep Auekarn.

38
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:54,380
This summary is based on the
committee's press release.

39
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:57,410
Meeting minutes and reports
are available through

40
00:02:57,410 --> 00:03:00,179
the channels of the
Secretariat of the Senate.

